n","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"64d902370bb28edb\" href=\"?note=64d902370bb28edb\" title=\"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction\">73-df-binary-many-one-reduction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"004d4e2ba3fdd14e\" href=\"?note=004d4e2ba3fdd14e\" title=\"73-df-dtm-language-decision\">73-df-dtm-language-decision</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_id","html":"HMU2007"},{"key":"source_ref","html":"§9.3, print pp. 390–401; PDF pp. 412–423; local typed effective reduction/coding"},{"key":"source_status","html":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate"},{"key":"reviewed_on","html":"2026-10-24"},{"key":"legacy_source_id","html":"HU1979"},{"key":"legacy_source_ref","html":"§8.4–8.7, pp. 185–207; local total computable reduction abstraction"},{"key":"legacy_source_status","html":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review"},{"key":"revision_round","html":"pdf-third-edition-20261024"},{"key":"edition_role","html":"third-edition-core"},{"key":"third_edition_chapter","html":"9"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq_m\">\\(\\leq_m\\)</span> (computable many-one reducibility, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"64d902370bb28edb\" href=\"?note=64d902370bb28edb\" title=\"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction\">73-df-binary-many-one-reduction</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\">\\(\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\\)</span> (decidable binary languages, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"004d4e2ba3fdd14e\" href=\"?note=004d4e2ba3fdd14e\" title=\"73-df-dtm-language-decision\">73-df-dtm-language-decision</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}decidability}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\n\\longrightarrow A\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}decidability}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\n\\longrightarrow A\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Compute a total reduction witness <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span> and run a decider for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B\">\\(B\\)</span> on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f(x)\">\\(f(x)\\)</span>. The defining biconditional for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq_m\">\\(\\leq_m\\)</span> gives the right answer, and totality of both computations gives halting on every input.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction","status":"resolved","id":"64d902370bb28edb","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dtm-language-decision","status":"resolved","id":"004d4e2ba3fdd14e","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-dtm-language-decision]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction","status":"resolved","id":"64d902370bb28edb","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\leq_m$ (computable many-one reducibility, see [[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction]])","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dtm-language-decision","status":"resolved","id":"004d4e2ba3fdd14e","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}$ (decidable binary languages, see [[73-df-dtm-language-decision]])","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"\\leq_m","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}decidability}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\n\\longrightarrow A\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"f","display":false},{"tex":"B","display":false},{"tex":"f(x)","display":false},{"tex":"\\leq_m","display":false}],"bytes":1834,"backlinks":[{"id":"6af52783a9bce985","anchor":"ref-216","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[73-thm-binary-reduction-decidability|Many-One Reduction Preserves Decidability Downward]]"},{"id":"8d80ca1aa93889a6","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["64d902370bb28edb","004d4e2ba3fdd14e"]}